(
  id: "retro-ps1",
  name: "Retro PS1",
  version: "1.0.0",
  category: Looks,
  description: "The PlayStation 1 look: a PS1 look file, eight tiny nearest-filtered materials with generated 32x32 and 64x64 textures, and a demo scene (two rooms and a corridor) with Gouraud lights, fog and a flickering lamp.",
  tags: ["ps1", "retro", "psx", "low-poly", "look", "materials"],
  author: "NLPA Collab",
  license: "MIT OR Apache-2.0",
  requires: ["fps-controller"],
  provides: [
    "retro-ps1/looks/ps1.look.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/brick.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/concrete.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/grass.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/metal_grate.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/skin.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/tile.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/water.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/materials/wood.mat.ron",
    "retro-ps1/textures/brick.png",
    "retro-ps1/textures/concrete.png",
    "retro-ps1/textures/grass.png",
    "retro-ps1/textures/metal_grate.png",
    "retro-ps1/textures/skin.png",
    "retro-ps1/textures/tile.png",
    "retro-ps1/textures/water.png",
    "retro-ps1/textures/wood.png",
    "scenes/retro-ps1/demo.scene.ron",
    "scripts/retro-ps1/lamp_flicker.lua",
  ],
  notes: "Open scenes/retro-ps1/demo.scene.ron and press Play (WASD, mouse). The look retro-ps1/looks/ps1.look.ron switches the retro render style on for any scene: Settings > Rendering > Look > Apply. Every knob is under Settings > Rendering > Retro / PS1: snap resolution (vertex jitter), affine strength and fade (texture swimming, fading out closer than 4 m), colour bits and dither (15-bit colour), vertex lighting, draw distance (the fog hides the cut), force nearest, internal resolution. The materials have Retro set to On, so they keep the look even in a scene that has it off; give UI or water materials Retro Off to keep them clean. The low internal resolution shows only in the game window on Full-tier GPUs, everything else shows in the editor viewport too. The corridor lamp's flicker script (scripts/retro-ps1/lamp_flicker.lua) parks the light out of range for moments, because scripts can't set light intensity yet. Textures are generated by library/tools/gen_retro_ps1.py.",
)
